 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The directory can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding a named specialty — an attribute the directory already shows — by naming that specialty in the page address. The whole specialty name matches and letter case is disregarded, while a name that is only the beginning of a specialty does not match. Naming a specialty no veterinarian holds returns the directory empty rather than failing, and naming nothing returns every veterinarian, as though no specialty had been named. When the narrowed directory runs to more than one page, moving between pages keeps the named specialty in effect. The same directory is also published in a machine-readable form at a second route, a supported surface that honors the same specialty filter `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened naming that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when the directory is opened, then it matches; given a name that is only the beginning of a held specialty, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened naming it, then a normal page is returned with no veterinarians listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty that is empty or only spaces, when the directory is opened, then every veterinarian is listed as though no specialty had been named.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed directory running to more than one page, when a later page is opened, then the named specialty is still in effect and only matching veterinarians are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the machine-readable list, when it is requested naming a specialty, then only the veterinarians holding that specialty are returned; when requested naming a specialty no veterinarian holds, then a normal response with no veterinarians is returned; when requested naming nothing, then every veterinarian is returned.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A second route publishes the same list in a machine-readable form. It is a supported surface under `[REQ-VET-003]` and honors the specialty filter; the withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` id is not reused (see the Superseded list).
+3. The specialty filter is reached through the page address only; this capability adds no on-page control. A visible control may follow as a separate request.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+**Design Rationale:** See [ADR: Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope; Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out](adr/2026-08-26-non-goal-vet-specialty-filter.md).
